parts.text:
Now SplitNavDemoTest. Need to add import `com.pathland.view.EnvironmentBinding` and change line 51.

Current imports:
```
import com.pathland.view.Categories;
import com.pathland.view.Commands;
import com.pathland.view.Components;
import com.pathland.view.Environment;
import com.pathland.view.Platform;
import com.pathland.view.Properties;
...
```
Add `import com.pathland.view.EnvironmentBinding;`.

Line 51: `new SplitNavDemo().environment(Platform.ACTIVE_PATH, activePath), env());`
→ `new SplitNavDemo().with(EnvironmentBinding.with(e -> e.key(Platform.ACTIVE_PATH).value(activePath))), env());`

Wait, `activePath` is `WritableSignal<String>`. The `value` overloads: `value(Object)` and `value(Signal<?>)`. Passing `WritableSignal<String>` → picks `value(Signal<?>)`. Good.

But careful: `EnvironmentBinding.with(e -> e.key(Platform.ACTIVE_PATH).value(activePath))` returns EnvironmentBinding (ViewModifier). Then `.with(...)` on SplitNavDemo plain View. Good.

Let me apply.

